        "id": 3485565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T07:45:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding Tomasz who has been working on kernel ownership model. From my side, please note this needs to be cherry-picked into the following branches as well:\n- android16-6.12-desktop\n- android-mainline-desktop",
      "revId": "34660ddc335d2b8988713f225cf436b5d9c157df",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f950cb0_924184b6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074825
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T07:46:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d propose keeping just one OWNERS file at the root of the source tree. While for the sound subsystem it\u0027s probably not a big deal, because it\u0027s all under one sound/ directory, many subsystems are split across different directories and we would run into a lot of OWNERS files scattered around, often with duplicate contents.\n\nAlso I\u0027d recommend setting a managed google group for the team (easily doable on teams/) instead of listing individual ldaps here, because from the ChromeOS experience, we often ended up with half or more entries pointing to people no longer working on the areas in question.",
      "revId": "34660ddc335d2b8988713f225cf436b5d9c157df",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71f4981d_5a86d584",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074825
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T08:22:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I just realized that Gerrit hasn\u0027t landed support for groups in OWNERS... The suggestion there seems to be to create a file with defined groups of individual emails and then include them in the OWNERS files. (Ref: https://android-review.googlesource.com/plugins/code-owners/Documentation/backend-find-owners.html#syntax:~:text\u003dis%20not%20possible.-,Groups,-Groups%20are%20not)",
      "parentUuid": "6f950cb0_924184b6",
      "revId": "34660ddc335d2b8988713f225cf436b5d9c157df",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f9230b5_100179ff",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2023081
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T08:26:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general while we can consider adding you to the OWNERS in 6.6, for 6.12 and further kernels it may not be the case at the very beginning.\n\nThe kernel/common repository since 6.12 is restricted in terms of patches which can be accepted and we want to keep monitoring them so only core or critical patches are being merged. People who are maintaining that are in the root OWNERS file.\n\nAs our goal is to reach GKI compatibility, we don\u0027t want to diverge too much from ACK. Plus we want people to slowly adapt the GKI model which is totally different from CrOS. That\u0027s the main reasons behind the OWNERS restrictions",
      "revId": "34660ddc335d2b8988713f225cf436b5d9c157df",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c79a5fc6_2391a426",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
